\ Test row variable tracking through words with unbalanced row vars

use "testing" ;

"row variable inference through while" test-section

\ while with simple pred/body validates correctly
uses-while: ( n -- n ) [ [ dup 10 < ] [ 1 + ] while ] ;
0 uses-while 10 "while loop" assert=

\ Row vars differing in size: pred pushes extra, body drops it
weird-while: ( n -- n n ) [ [ dup dup 10 < ] [ drop 1 + ] while ] ;
0 weird-while 10 "weird while extra" assert= 10 "weird while val" assert=

"row variable inference through if" test-section

\ if with matched branches
choose: ( n -- n ) [ dup 5 > [ 1 + ] [ 1 - ] if ] ;
3 choose 2 "if below threshold" assert=
7 choose 8 "if above threshold" assert=

"when with intentional no-op false branch" test-section

\ when uses [ ] as false branch; constraint conflict is handled gracefully
maybe-inc: ( n ? -- n ) [ [ 1 + ] when ] ;
5 t maybe-inc 6 "when true" assert=
5 f maybe-inc 5 "when false" assert=

"row var validation catches mismatches" test-section

\ Body delta inconsistent with pred delta:
\ pred pushes 1 value (delta=+1), which means ..b - ..a = 0
\ body pushes 1 value (delta=+1), which means ..a - ..b = +1, i.e., ..b - ..a = -1
\ These conflict, so the body should fail validation
[ 0 [ dup 10 < ] [ dup 1 + ] while ] "while body leaves extra value" assert-error
